# llama.cpp server hosting Zoe's local voice brain — Gemma 4 E4B-QAT + MTP, port 11434.
#
# This mirrors the live Zoe config (the "brain" rock — see docs/CANONICAL.md). It is
# platform-specific; before installing, set:
#   - the llama-server binary path (built for your platform / GPU)
#   - the --model + --model-draft paths to your downloaded GGUFs
# See HARDWARE_COMPATIBILITY.md and scripts/setup/download_gguf_models.sh.
#
# BUILD + FLAGS (B0.4, 2026-09-27 — llama.cpp b11194, commit 9f70b2cec):
#   - Built from source with GGML_CUDA=ON, CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=87, GGML_CUDA_FA=ON,
#     GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS=ON, GGML_NATIVE=ON, Release (the prebuilt arm64 asset is CUDA 13.x,
#     not JetPack's 12.6 — source build is mandatory) into ~/llama.cpp-b11194/build-jetson.
#   - FlashAttention is ON with the MTP drafter. On the old b9733 build FA crashed in
#     fattn.cu with draft-mtp (fixed upstream in #25148, 2026-06-30). FA on is what
#     unlocks a quantized V cache: K AND V are both q8_0 here (a quantized V cache
#     without FA throws at startup — llama-context.cpp).
#   - Replay-gated in two brain windows on 2026-09-27 (Gemma 4 E4B-QAT + MTP, FA on):
#       A) K q8_0 / V q8_0 -> replay PASS 11/11 scoreable, 0 fail, brain median 1754 ms, 0 errors
#       B) K q8_0 / V f16  -> replay PASS 11/11 scoreable, 0 fail, brain median 1752.5 ms, 0 errors
#     A is adopted: same latency, smaller KV cache = more headroom on 15.6G unified memory.
#   - Flag renames in this build: `--mlock` is GONE -> `--load-mode mmap+mlock`;
#     `--chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking":false}'` is deprecated -> `--reasoning off`.
#   - SINGLE SLOT (--parallel 1) — correctness over concurrency. Upstream
#     ggml-org/llama.cpp#28286 (OPEN, filed 2026-09-03): draft-MTP with --parallel > 1
#     leaks content BETWEEN concurrent requests' prompts/completions, with no
#     garbage-token signature to detect it by. The unit ran --parallel 2 before B0.4,
#     so the live brain has been exposed. With one slot, concurrent requests queue
#     instead of running side by side, and the whole --ctx-size belongs to that one
#     slot. Do NOT raise --parallel while --spec-type draft-mtp is set, until
#     #28286 is fixed AND replay-gated here.
#   - --fit off is explicit: b11194 (and b9733) default --fit ON, which adjusts unset
#     arguments to fit device memory. The B0.4 gate keeps it off, so the serving
#     config is exactly what is written below.
#
# ROLLBACK (to the b9733 build, FA off): point ExecStart AND LD_LIBRARY_PATH back at
#   %h/llama.cpp/build-jetson-new/bin, set `--flash-attn off`, DROP `--cache-type-v`
#   (V must be f16 with FA off), replace `--load-mode mmap+mlock` with `--mlock`, and
#   replace `--reasoning off` with `--chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking":false}'`
#   (b9733 has neither --load-mode nor --reasoning). KEEP --parallel 1 and --fit off on
#   rollback (#28286 is build-independent; b9733 accepts both). Then daemon-reload + restart in a
#   Kokoro-paused window. Full recipe: docs/knowledge/voice-pipeline.md.
[Unit]
Description=llama.cpp Server for Zoe (Gemma 4 E4B-QAT + MTP — live voice brain)
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
LimitMEMLOCK=infinity

# ── Keep the brain rock resident ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# `--load-mode mmap+mlock` below (was `--mlock` before b11194) asks llama.cpp to
# lock the weights; LimitMEMLOCK=infinity lets
# it. That is necessary but NOT sufficient — measured 2026-07-18 on the live
# Orin, VmLck held only 1.95 GB of a 5.6 GB RSS and 1,457 MB had still been
# swapped out (mlock covers the mapped model, not every CUDA/unified-memory
# allocation around it on Tegra).
#
# MemoryLow is soft (reclaim-resistant, not swap-proof), which is why it alone
# did not stop the eviction. MemorySwapMax=0 is the hard line for the pages
# mlock does not reach.
#
# MemoryLow was previously a LOCAL drop-in only (~/.config/systemd/user/
# llama-server.service.d/memory.conf) — real protection that existed on one box
# and in no template, so a rebuild or a second host silently lost it. Tracked
# here now. Same story for CPUWeight/IOWeight from priority.conf.
#
# NOTE: this is a ~5.6 GB RSS process. MemorySwapMax=0 removes its release
# valve, so pressure surfaces as an OOM kill instead of silent slow paging —
# which is the intended trade for the brain rock (a swapped brain is a broken
# brain), but it is why no MemoryMax is set here: a hard ceiling plus no swap
# would turn a transient spike into a kill. See docs/knowledge/voice-pipeline.md.
#
# No Nice=-N / OOMScoreAdjust=-N: a --user unit cannot raise priority on this
# box (`ulimit -e` is 0) and systemd SILENTLY DROPS the value while reporting
# success — verified 2026-07-18 (Nice=-5 applied as 0). Dev tooling
# de-prioritises itself instead (serena-mcp.service: Nice=10), which works
# because positive values need no privilege.
MemorySwapMax=0
MemoryLow=6G
CPUWeight=400
IOWeight=400
# The ExecStartPost health probe waits up to 120s for model+draft load; raise the
# start timeout above it so systemd doesn't kill the unit at the 90s default first.
TimeoutStartSec=180
# Point LD_LIBRARY_PATH at the directory of your llama.cpp build.
Environment=LD_LIBRARY_PATH=%h/llama.cpp-b11194/build-jetson/bin
# The endpoint is unauthenticated. Default to loopback; the live Zoe host binds
# 0.0.0.0 ONLY because it is fronted by Cloudflare Access + host firewalling. Do NOT
# expose 0.0.0.0 without equivalent auth/firewalling.
# KV-cache tuning (2026-07-21, evidence in docs/knowledge/brain-kv-cache-tuning.md):
#  --ctx-size 8192 --parallel 1  = ONE 8192 slot (B6.6, 2026-09-27). 8192 is the
#    per-slot size the brain served from 2026-07-21 to B0.4 (16384 / --parallel 2),
#    and it is the window the Flue brain client already budgets for
#    (labs/flue-zoe-brain-2x/src/context-window.ts DEFAULT_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS =
#    8192 incl. a 1536-token reply reserve) — a 16384 slot bought nothing it can use.
#    Measured 36 h of live traffic (630 turns): prompt+reply p50 2852 / p99 3280 /
#    max 3338 tokens. Saves ~170 MiB RSS at load (~120 MiB after traffic), replay
#    PASS; evidence in docs/knowledge/brain-flags-tuning-2026-09.md. Never set it
#    below the Flue window (tests/unit/test_llama_server_unit_flags.py pins that).
#    The 2026-07-21 tuning ran --parallel 2 (two 8192 slots, so voice + chat kept
#    separate warm prefixes); it was dropped for correctness: #28286 (header above).
#    The --cache-ram host prompt cache below is what now keeps every prefix warm.
#  --cache-ram 2048  = the Oct-2025 host-memory prompt cache (PR #16391),
#    similarity hot-swap of whole cached prompts; SWA-compatible. Default is
#    8192 MiB — on this 15.6G UNIFIED-memory box that default is an OOM
#    hazard, so it is capped. Never remove the cap. It is a CAP, not a
#    reservation: entries are allocated lazily and evicted oldest-first at the
#    cap. With ONE slot it is load-bearing — every chat turn rotates ~5 prompts
#    (main turn + aux one-shots) through the slot, and --cache-ram 0 measured
#    +4.1 s TTFT on every repeat chat turn (B6.6). Do not lower it without a
#    24 h occupancy measurement (entries carry up to 32 SWA checkpoints of
#    ~10.6 MiB each, so one ~2.8k-token turn is ~170 MiB).
#  --flash-attn on + K AND V at q8_0 (B0.4, b11194): FA with the MTP draft is
#    fixed upstream (#25148) and replay-gated here (header above). FA on is the
#    precondition for the quantized V cache; V at q8_0 halves the ~4 global
#    layers' V cost vs f16 (~32MB at 8192 -> ~16MB). If FA must go OFF again
#    (rollback), V MUST go back to f16 (drop --cache-type-v) or startup throws.
#  --cache-reuse OMITTED BY CHOICE — not because it would be ignored (corrected
#    2026-08-03). Upstream #21468 was closed as fixed by #22288 (2026-04-24) and
#    that fix is in this build; get_can_shift() has no Gemma exclusion. It is
#    CONDITIONALLY off: llama_kv_cache_iswa::get_can_shift() requires
#    kv_base->get_size() == kv_swa->get_size(), and SWA layers are sized by the
#    512-token window. --swa-full equalises them and re-enables --cache-reuse,
#    but that IS ~50x SWA cache growth (30MiB -> 1536MiB measured on Gemma E2B)
#    — unaffordable on 15.6G unified memory. So exact common-prefix reuse + the
#    host prompt cache above is the strategy, which makes prompt-prefix
#    stability load-bearing: see services/zoe-data/AGENTS.md ("mutate the tail,
#    never the head"). Do NOT add --cache-reuse without also budgeting --swa-full.
ExecStart=%h/llama.cpp-b11194/build-jetson/bin/llama-server \
  --model %h/models/gemma4-e4b-qat/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf \
  --model-draft %h/models/gemma4-e4b-qat/mtp-gemma-4-E4B-it.gguf \
  --spec-type draft-mtp \
  --spec-draft-n-max 4 \
  --spec-draft-p-min 0.6 \
  --spec-draft-ngl 99 \
  --host 127.0.0.1 \
  --port 11434 \
  --ctx-size 8192 \
  --parallel 1 \
  --cache-type-k q8_0 \
  --cache-type-v q8_0 \
  --cache-ram 2048 \
  --n-gpu-layers 99 \
  --cont-batching \
  --fit off \
  --flash-attn on \
  --temp 0.7 \
  --top-k 64 \
  --top-p 0.95 \
  --jinja \
  --reasoning off \
  --load-mode mmap+mlock \
  --metrics
# Block until /health says ok (model + draft load), or fail the unit after 120s.
ExecStartPost=/bin/bash -c 'for i in $(seq 1 120); do curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:11434/health 2>/dev/null | grep -q ok && exit 0; sleep 1; done; exit 1'
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=10
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
